1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,169
Previously, on Friends...

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:03,420
How did the
job stuff go?

3
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:05,213
He offered me one.

4
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:08,175
You know what? This calls for
a bottle of Israel's finest.

5
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:12,805
The job is in Paris.

6
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:21,104
Oh God, please,
somebody say something.

7
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:23,524
So, if you take this job,
you'll be...

8
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:25,275
you'll be moving to Paris?

9
00:00:25,317 --> 00:00:27,528
Or facing a bitch of a commute.

10
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,571
I know,
I know...

11
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:31,323
It's huge, and it's scary

12
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:34,368
and it's really far, far away
from you guys.

13
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:37,872
But this is such an incredible
opportunity for me.

14
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:39,289
And I've already talked
to them

15
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:40,624
about our situation
with Emma.

16
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,125
And they said they'll do

17
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,919
whatever we need
to make us feel comfortable.

18
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:45,128
Okay.

19
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,839
I mean, I'll fly
back and forth.

20
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:49,008
They'll fly you out,
anything we want.

21
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:52,219
My boss said I might be getting
a new lamp in my cubicle.

22
00:00:57,725 --> 00:00:59,059
All right.

23
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,019
We'll work it out.

24
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:00,936
Oh, thank you!

25
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:01,937
Thank you!

26
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:02,938
Yeah.

27
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,231
Oh!

28
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,942
You sure this
is what you want?

29
00:01:06,984 --> 00:01:08,527
I think it is.

30
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,237
( chuckles )

31
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,324
Ooh, what's going on?

32
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:16,869
I got a really incredible
job offer.

33
00:01:16,911 --> 00:01:18,119
Hey, great!
Good for you!

34
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,162
All right!

35
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:20,455
It's in Paris.

36
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:25,084
What?! No! No! No!
No! No! No! No! No! No!

37
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:27,086
Too much is changing, okay?

38
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:29,130
First Phoebe getting married!

39
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,591
Congratulations.

40
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,175
And then... and then these two

41
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:34,720
moving to a stupid house
in the stupid suburbs!

42
00:01:34,762 --> 00:01:36,597
Hey! This afternoon,
you said you'd be supportive.

43
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,933
Well, it comes and goes!
I wouldn't trust it!

44
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:43,729
Well, you guys, this is really,
really important to me,

45
00:01:43,771 --> 00:01:46,273
and it means a lot
if you can try to get on board.

46
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:47,733
Of course we can.
Congratulations.

47
00:01:47,775 --> 00:01:48,901
Thank you.
Yay!

48
00:01:48,943 --> 00:01:49,902
Oh!

49
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:51,070
Joey?

50
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:52,654
No, no, no!
No, no.

51
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:55,282
My hugs are reserved for people
staying in America!

52
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:57,576
Joey, it would mean...

53
00:01:57,618 --> 00:02:00,412
Hey, no, hey, get your
France-going arms away from me!

54
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:04,083
Are you okay with this?

55
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,043
Well, it makes me
feel sad, but...

56
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:08,003
Talking to Ross.
I see.

57
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:12,549
Well, Rachel moving
to another country?

58
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:14,635
Not being able to see her
every day?

59
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,470
How could I be okay with this?

60
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,263
I know, but what are we
gonna do?

61
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:19,765
She really needs this job.

62
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:22,434
Do you think if, uh...
if the Ralph Lauren people

63
00:02:22,476 --> 00:02:25,020
offered her her old job back,
she would take it?

64
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,730
Well, how is that
going to happen?

65
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:29,775
Is this the best way
to use one of your
three magic wishes?

66
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:32,111
Like, I don't know.
I could talk to her boss.

67
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,403
Yeah!

68
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:35,072
I met him
at that Christmas party.

69
00:02:35,114 --> 00:02:36,782
I mean, we really hit it off.

70
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:38,617
You mean, the guy
who kept calling you "Ron"?

71
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:40,619
I didn't say we were brothers!

72
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:52,089
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

73
00:02:52,131 --> 00:02:54,800
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

74
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:56,969
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

75
00:02:57,011 --> 00:03:02,099
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

76
00:03:02,141 --> 00:03:04,434
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

77
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:06,895
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

78
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:10,607
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

79
00:03:10,649 --> 00:03:16,363
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

80
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,200
Hey, Phoebe?
Hi!

81
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,870
Hey, um, tell me
what you think.

82
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,579
All right, the house
next door to the one

83
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:26,915
that we're buying in Westchester
just went on the market.

84
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:29,250
Now, I want to take a look
at it, but Chandler doesn't.

85
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:32,754
We close escrow tomorrow,
so seeing another house
can only confuse us.

86
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:35,298
And we're easily confused.
We're not very bright.

87
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,135
But what if it's better
than ours?

88
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:39,469
Shouldn't we at least look?

89
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,013
What do you
think, Pheebs?

90
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:42,973
Well, I think that shirt
makes you look

91
00:03:43,015 --> 00:03:45,433
like you should work
at a Baskin-Robbins.

92
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:50,271
Anyway...

93
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,860
Hey, isn't Joey's agent
Estelle Leonard?

94
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:56,153
Yeah.

95
00:03:56,195 --> 00:03:57,154
She died.

96
00:03:57,196 --> 00:03:58,155
You're kidding.

97
00:03:58,197 --> 00:03:59,322
That's terrible.

98
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,324
Yeah, last Saturday.

99
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:05,370
Wow! She was the first black man
to fly solo across the Atlantic!

100
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:09,750
Oh, wait a minute.
I read the wrong one.

101
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,710
Oh, yeah?

102
00:04:11,752 --> 00:04:13,795
Yeah, she was just an agent.

103
00:04:13,837 --> 00:04:16,215
Joey's going to be
so upset.

104
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:20,510
I know. He always wanted
to be the first black man
to cross the Atlantic.

105
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,430
Well, we cannot tell Joey
about this.

106
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:26,016
He's already flipping out about
everything that's changing.

107
00:04:26,058 --> 00:04:27,475
This'll push him over the edge.

108
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,978
Seriously, you don't think
we should tell him?

109
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,688
Well, not for a little while.

110
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,399
Let's just give him a few days
to get used to everything else.

111
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:36,401
Well, what if he reads it
in the paper?

112
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:39,863
Unless Snoopy says it
to Charlie Brown, I
think we're okay.

113
00:04:46,078 --> 00:04:47,704
May I help you?

114
00:04:47,746 --> 00:04:49,623
Yeah. I'm a friend
of Rachel Green's.

115
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:52,000
Um, actually, we-we met
at the Christmas party

116
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:53,043
about two years ago.

117
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:54,920
Oh, right. Uh, Don?

118
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:56,588
Close. Ron.

119
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:01,218
Well, uh...
what can I do for you?

120
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:02,928
Um, well, I'm here to see

121
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:05,889
if-if, uh, you'll give
Rachel her job back.

122
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:09,184
Ah, did she ask you
to come here and do this?

123
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:11,145
Oh, no. First, I have
to get you to agree.

124
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:13,147
Then we'll see
if she wants to come back.

125
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:16,900
Wow. That is tempting.

126
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,652
Look, she loved her job here.

127
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:21,571
And let's face it,
you're not going to find anyone

128
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:23,406
who did it as well as she did.

129
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:24,950
Isn't that true?

130
00:05:24,992 --> 00:05:26,785
She is good.

131
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:29,204
Huh. I took a shot there.

132
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:32,082
But I'm sorry,
there's nothing I can do.

133
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:35,961
Well, that's not true.
There's nothing I want to do.

134
00:05:36,003 --> 00:05:38,337
I see.

135
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:40,632
Thanks very much.

136
00:05:40,674 --> 00:05:41,758
Mm-hmm.

137
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,306
Is this your son?

138
00:05:47,346 --> 00:05:48,849
Yeah.
His name is Ross.

139
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:54,271
What?

140
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:56,648
Uh, nothing.
It's just... it's, uh...

141
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:58,025
it's close to "Ron".

142
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:01,862
Does he, um...

143
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:04,281
does little Ross like dinosaurs,
by any chance?

144
00:06:04,323 --> 00:06:06,365
Yeah, they're all
he talks about. Why?

145
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:10,204
How would he like to come
with me

146
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:12,789
to the Museum
of Natural History,

147
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:16,835
after everyone else has left--
just the two of us--

148
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:19,671
and he can touch
anything he wants?

149
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:27,346
I just heard it
how you must have heard it,

150
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:28,471
and that's not good.

151
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:29,806
Um, let me start again.

152
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:30,974
I'm a paleontologist.

153
00:06:31,016 --> 00:06:32,934
Uh, you'll be
there with us.

154
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:37,105
And the touching refers
only to bones-- fossils!

155
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:41,526
You could really
arrange that?

156
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:44,154
You let Rachel come back,
and it's done.

157
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:45,446
Well...

158
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:46,907
I guess having Rachel back

159
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:48,825
wouldn't be the worst thing
in the world.

160
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:49,993
Yes! Oh, thank you!

161
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:51,828
This is great.
Thank you so much.

162
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:55,165
And I swear, your kid's going
to have the time of his life.

163
00:06:55,207 --> 00:06:56,917
That's great.
I worry about little Ross.

164
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,835
He's always reading,
he's collecting rocks,

165
00:06:58,877 --> 00:07:00,295
and he's obsessed
with dinosaurs.

166
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,546
He'll be fine!

167
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:05,133
Hey, Pheebs.

168
00:07:05,175 --> 00:07:06,176
Hey.

169
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:07,594
Everything okay?

170
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:09,596
I'm just mad at my agent.

171
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:11,390
Estelle? Why?

172
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,267
Well, there's a part
in this TV movie

173
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:14,726
that I would be perfect for,

174
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,519
and I didn't even
get put up for it.

175
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,105
She better have
a good reason.

176
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:21,775
I'm guessing she does.

177
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:25,695
Yeah, well... I wanna
hear it, because she
keeps doing this.

178
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:27,197
Well, no, wait, wait, wait!

179
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:28,823
I... all right,
I-I got to go.

180
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,242
Just listen.
Promise me

181
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:32,702
that you will wait a minute
before you call her.

182
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:34,621
Oh, okay. Why?

183
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:37,498
Because a promise
between friends

184
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:40,752
means never having
to give a reason.

185
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:47,801
I love that saying!

186
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,677
( muttering )

187
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:54,724
( cell phone rings )

188
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:56,435
Hello?

189
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:59,354
( in gruff voice ):
Joey, it's Estelle.

190
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:01,189
I was just gonna call you.

191
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:02,607
That's weird.

192
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:06,611
It's a little coincidental,
but believable.

193
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,740
Listen,
I'm sure you're wondering

194
00:08:10,782 --> 00:08:13,910
why I didn't get you
an audition for that TV movie.

195
00:08:13,952 --> 00:08:15,412
Yeah, actually, I am.

196
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:17,622
I guess I dropped
the ball there.

197
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,749
Whoopsy!

198
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:21,542
That's it?!

199
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:24,338
You know, it seems like all
you do lately is drop the ball.

200
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:26,340
Don't take that tone with me.

201
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:28,091
Who do you think you are?

202
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:32,595
Alan Lemon, the first black man
to fly solo across the Atlantic?

203
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,017
No-No. Look, all I'm saying is,
you're my agent, okay?

204
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:39,102
And you're not getting me
into any auditions,

205
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:40,437
and I'm tired of it!

206
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:41,771
What are you saying?

207
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:42,981
I'm saying that...

208
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:45,108
this isn't working
for me anymore.

209
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:47,652
Okay, Estelle?
You're fired. Good-bye.

210
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:52,782
Man!
Tough week for Estelle.

211
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:56,786
Hi.

212
00:08:56,828 --> 00:08:58,205
Hi.

213
00:08:58,246 --> 00:09:00,499
Emma left her stuffed T-rex
at my house.

214
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,667
You know she can't
sleep without it.

215
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:04,961
Ah, well, she's asleep now.

216
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:07,506
Stop forcing that thing on her.

217
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,548
Okay.

218
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:10,300
Oh! You're not
gonna believe

219
00:09:10,342 --> 00:09:11,926
what happened
to me today!

220
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:15,180
Ralph Lauren called
and gave me my job back.

221
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:16,181
No!

222
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:17,974
Yeah!

223
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:19,726
I mean,
it was the weirdest thing.

224
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,644
They fire me,
and then out of nowhere,

225
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,355
they just hire me back.

226
00:09:23,397 --> 00:09:25,815
I mean, that place must just be
falling apart without me.

227
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:27,567
So, you're not
going to Paris?

228
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:29,403
No, I'm still going!

229
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:31,071
What?!

230
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,364
Ooh!

231
00:09:32,406 --> 00:09:33,656
( chuckling )

232
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:36,159
What?!

233
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:38,661
Well, when the Louis Vuitton
people found out

234
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,455
that Ralph Lauren
wanted me back,

235
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:41,998
they offered me more money.

236
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,833
Isn't that great?!

237
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,336
Yay!

238
00:09:46,378 --> 00:09:48,547
Whoo!

239
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:52,675
( knocking at door )

240
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,803
Hi. We're buying
the house next door,

241
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,473
and we were wondering if we
could just take a look around.

242
00:09:58,515 --> 00:10:01,684
Oh, sure! I'm showing it
to someone else right now,
but please, look around.

243
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,186
Thanks.

244
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:05,188
I feel like we're cheating
on our house.

245
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,690
And if we're gonna cheat,
shouldn't it be with, like,

246
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:10,693
a hot, younger house that does
stuff that our house won't do?

247
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,613
Wow!

248
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:16,366
Ours is so much better.

249
00:10:16,408 --> 00:10:17,992
This living room
is smaller.

250
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:20,370
The dining room
looks like a cave.

251
00:10:20,412 --> 00:10:21,704
What a hole!

252
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:22,997
So... what do you think?

253
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,708
Love it! Yeah.

254
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,544
Well, we already have
one offer on it,

255
00:10:27,586 --> 00:10:29,670
and I think the lady upstairs
is going to make another one.

256
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,756
They could be our neighbors.
What are they like?

257
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:33,425
Oh, the woman upstairs
is very nice.

258
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:35,051
She and her husband
have two kids.

259
00:10:35,093 --> 00:10:37,220
Uh he's on Wall Street,
and she's...

260
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:41,475
Oh... my... God!

261
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,193
Sure.

262
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,408
( knocking on door )

263
00:10:58,450 --> 00:11:00,368
Hey, Joey, you want
to come with me to...

264
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:01,786
Are you okay?

265
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,079
Yeah, I just...

266
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:05,039
I just feel bad
about firing Estelle.

267
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:06,791
This has got to be killing her.

268
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:09,961
( clears throat )

269
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:12,880
No. That wouldn't kill her.

270
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,716
A coronary embolism might.

271
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,552
I don't know.
She's got to be taking it hard.

272
00:11:17,594 --> 00:11:18,761
I was, like,
her only client.

273
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,013
Mm-hmm.

274
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,640
Except for this guy
who eats paper.

275
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,476
And I'm guessing he eats
more money than he makes.

276
00:11:26,311 --> 00:11:27,728
Look, I know
she's not a great agent,

277
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,356
but she did stick with me
for ten years.

278
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,609
I'm gonna call her
and hire her again.

279
00:11:32,651 --> 00:11:33,692
No, no, no!

280
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:34,861
Don't-Don't call her.

281
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,530
You wait for her to call you.

282
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:38,615
Why?

283
00:11:38,657 --> 00:11:44,829
Because patience is the road
to understanding...

284
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:48,542
which is the key
to a happy heart.

285
00:11:50,877 --> 00:11:53,380
You blow me away.

286
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,674
All, right, so promise
you're going to wait

287
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:56,799
for her to call you?

288
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,301
I promise.
Okay.

289
00:11:58,343 --> 00:12:02,138
And that means...
never having to give a reason.

290
00:12:05,308 --> 00:12:08,395
What a small world.

291
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:11,690
And yet I never run
into Beyonce.

292
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,026
You two know each other?

293
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,528
Oh, we go way back.

294
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:18,321
Before Monica made
an honest man out of him,

295
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:21,157
Chandler used to be
my little love muffin.

296
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:22,783
( braying laughter )

297
00:12:24,619 --> 00:12:26,871
So, are you guys thinking
of getting this house, too?

298
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:28,665
Ooh, are we going to have
a bidding war?

299
00:12:28,707 --> 00:12:30,166
I better warn you,
I'm a toughie.

300
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:31,834
( braying laughter)
Don't... Don't...

301
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,545
Don't!

302
00:12:33,587 --> 00:12:35,338
No, actually,
we're buying the
house next door.

303
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,005
( delighted gasp )

304
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:38,091
Why?

305
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,554
I don't know why.

306
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:44,180
Ooh, that decides it then.

307
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:45,806
I was on the fence,

308
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:48,351
but knowing that you two
would be our neighbors...

309
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,353
( shrieks )...
now we have to get it!

310
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:51,896
Ellen,

311
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,648
we're going to talk numbers.

312
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:54,982
( braying chuckle )

313
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,154
This cannot be happening.

314
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,615
Okay, the Realtor said

315
00:13:01,656 --> 00:13:03,450
another couple
made an offer.

316
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,993
Maybe the Janices won't get it.

317
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:08,288
Maybe the other
couple will.

318
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,789
The only way that that is going
to happen is

319
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,875
if the other couple are
the Hitlers.

320
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:17,213
Okay, okay.

321
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:18,797
All right, what if we get
both houses?

322
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:20,841
Huh? We can turn this house
into a guest house.

323
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:22,427
That's a great idea.

324
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:24,512
And, by the way, and I don't
mean to be distasteful,

325
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:27,014
but when did you
start crapping money?

326
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:28,683
Okay, you come up with an idea.

327
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,351
All right,
all right, all right.

328
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:31,978
We've still got three hours

329
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:34,021
until escrow closes
on our house.

330
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,398
We can still get out.

331
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,899
But we love our house.

332
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,610
Will we love it so much
with her next door?

333
00:13:38,652 --> 00:13:41,070
And she's going to be
louder out here, too.

334
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:44,783
Just the crickets and
"Oh... my... God!"

335
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:46,660
Okay. But if we don't get
this house,

336
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:48,953
she's still going to show up
wherever we go.

337
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:50,580
I mean, at least if she's here,

338
00:13:50,622 --> 00:13:52,540
it eliminates the element
of surprise.

339
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:55,460
I mean, never again will you
have to hear the three words

340
00:13:55,502 --> 00:13:58,171
that make your balls jump
back up inside your body.

341
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:05,303
Well, we have to do something.

342
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,180
We can't have her living
next door.

343
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:11,476
( braying laughter )

344
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:14,020
Ah, that does it, too.

345
00:14:19,484 --> 00:14:20,819
( knocking on door )

346
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,111
Who is it?

347
00:14:22,153 --> 00:14:23,988
It's me... Ron.

348
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,157
( sighs )

349
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,660
Look, I, uh, I know
Rachel turned you down,

350
00:14:28,702 --> 00:14:30,161
but I think there's a way

351
00:14:30,203 --> 00:14:32,580
you might be able
to get her to come back.

352
00:14:32,622 --> 00:14:34,332
This may surprise you,

353
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:38,169
but rehiring fired employees
is not my main job.

354
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:39,170
Well...

355
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:40,839
Just hear me out.

356
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:45,301
How would you feel
about offering her a raise?

357
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,516
Not good, Ron.

358
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:55,061
Perhaps I can
persuade you.

359
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:58,648
What if you could
give your son this...

360
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:03,902
genuine pterodactyl egg replica?

361
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,995
Wow. That's, uh,
that's pretty cool.

362
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:16,666
Yeah? So... do we have a deal?

363
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:18,793
Okay, you got it.

364
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:20,420
Yes! Yes.

365
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:22,547
This is going to make me
very popular.

366
00:15:22,589 --> 00:15:23,840
Oh... ( chuckles )

367
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:26,259
Believe me, the ladies,
they love it.

368
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,015
I meant with my son.

369
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:35,602
Good, 'cause the ladies,
not so much.

370
00:15:43,818 --> 00:15:46,987
MAN ( on machine ):
Joey, this is Al Zeebooker,

371
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:49,574
the guy who eats paper.

372
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:53,411
I'm sure you've heard
that Estelle passed away.

373
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:56,289
I wanted to let you know
there's a memorial for her,

374
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,583
at the Westside Chapel,
tomorrow at 10:00.

375
00:15:58,625 --> 00:16:01,127
Hope you can make it.

376
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:04,505
Oh, my God.

377
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:08,259
( phone rings )

378
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:11,638
( beeps )

379
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,222
Hello.

380
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:15,809
( Estelle's voice ):
Joey, it's Estelle.

381
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:22,315
Estelle?

382
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:23,483
Yeah.

383
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,401
I wanted to call and tell you

384
00:16:25,443 --> 00:16:28,321
that there's no hard feelings
for firing me.

385
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:34,535
Okay.

386
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:36,996
I just, I can't believe
you're calling me.

387
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:39,165
Well, I didn't think
I should just drop by.

388
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:41,960
No, no! Don't drop by!
Don't drop by!

389
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,837
Don't, don't, no, no...

390
00:16:43,878 --> 00:16:44,879
Anyway,

391
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,965
you did what you had to do.

392
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,132
I'm okay.

393
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:49,383
Uh, c-can I ask you something?

394
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,678
Um...

395
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:53,179
What's it like there?

396
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:55,974
It's all right.

397
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,892
Look, kiddo,

398
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:00,854
I got to go.
Good luck with the career.

399
00:17:00,895 --> 00:17:02,522
You're gonna be huge.

400
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,231
Thanks for everything, Estelle.

401
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,484
Bye.

402
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:07,694
( beeps )

403
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:09,487
"Out of area."

404
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:10,947
Boy, I'll say!

405
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:19,205
Well...
I just talked to Sid.

406
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:22,625
We are definitely putting
in an offer on the house.

407
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:24,168
And I'll bet we get it!

408
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:27,672
The Hitlers will be
so disappointed.

409
00:17:27,714 --> 00:17:29,674
All right, I-I got to run.

410
00:17:29,716 --> 00:17:31,843
Tell Monica I say good-bye.

411
00:17:31,885 --> 00:17:33,511
And... I'll see you later.

412
00:17:33,553 --> 00:17:35,513
Neighbor...
( braying laughter )

413
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:37,807
Wait!

414
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,059
I just want you to know that...

415
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,729
I'm so happy
you're going to be here.

416
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:43,938
Oh! Me too!

417
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:44,939
( laughs )

418
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:46,440
Because!

419
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:52,613
That way... we can pick up
where we left off.

420
00:17:55,742 --> 00:17:56,701
Huh?

421
00:17:56,743 --> 00:17:59,286
I never stopped loving you.

422
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,621
Oh... my...

423
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:02,248
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

424
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:08,046
I want you... I need you.

425
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:14,052
I must have you, Janice
Litman-Goralnik nee Hosenstein.

426
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:20,391
Chandler, what are
you talking about?

427
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:24,395
Now that you live next door,
we can be together every day.

428
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:27,314
Sid and Monica
never have to know a thing.

429
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:29,067
I don't know
what to say.

430
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:32,653
I mean, you know,
obviously...

431
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:36,574
we have this...
heat between us.

432
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:43,539
Obviously.

433
00:18:43,581 --> 00:18:46,751
But I love my husband.

434
00:18:46,793 --> 00:18:49,045
And I know you love your wife.

435
00:18:49,087 --> 00:18:52,339
I-I don't think
we should get this house now

436
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:56,552
Don't say that. Don't dangle
the dream, then take it away.

437
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:57,804
Chandler,

438
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:00,431
one of us has
got to be strong.

439
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:03,059
I understand.

440
00:19:03,101 --> 00:19:06,980
Although...

441
00:19:07,021 --> 00:19:09,983
maybe just...
one last moment of weakness.

442
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,943
( grunts )

443
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:16,656
( sighs )

444
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:25,999
Good-bye, Chandler Bing.

445
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:34,007
( strained ):
They're never coming down now.

446
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:36,968
( knocking )
Hi.

447
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:38,011
Hi.

448
00:19:38,052 --> 00:19:40,138
You are never
going to believe

449
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,305
what happened
to me today.

450
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:42,640
What?

451
00:19:42,682 --> 00:19:44,017
Ralph Lauren called,

452
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:46,477
again, and they offered me
more money.

453
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:47,728
They did?!

454
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:48,980
Yes.

455
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,482
It was the weirdest thing.

456
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:52,859
Zelner called me
and he said,

457
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,986
"We will do anything
we can to get you back,"

458
00:19:55,028 --> 00:19:57,155
and that I should thank
some Ron.

459
00:19:57,196 --> 00:20:00,324
I don't even know what
department that guy's in.

460
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:01,826
( stammers )

461
00:20:01,868 --> 00:20:03,911
So, what are you,
what are you going to do?

462
00:20:03,953 --> 00:20:05,329
Well, I took it.

463
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:07,456
That's great.
So you're staying in New York.

464
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:10,168
( both cheering )

465
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:11,544
Yay... uh...

466
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:13,880
You're-You're
excited, right?

467
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:15,173
Yeah... Yeah.

468
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,716
The money's great.

469
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:19,510
It's certainly
the easier choice.

470
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:21,261
Right.

471
00:20:21,303 --> 00:20:24,932
But you know, was I looking
forward to going to Paris? Sure.

472
00:20:24,974 --> 00:20:27,518
You know, was I excited
about working

473
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:30,021
in the fashion capital
of the world?

474
00:20:30,063 --> 00:20:31,480
Oh, absolutely!

475
00:20:31,522 --> 00:20:34,358
( sighs )

476
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:39,279
Yeah, but, you know, this is...
it's fine.

477
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:43,617
I'm fine going back to a job
where I've pretty much gotten

478
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:47,163
everything out of it
that I possibly can.

479
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:49,665
( sighs )

480
00:20:49,707 --> 00:20:52,585
Um... I had no...

481
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:59,425
I had no idea you were,
you were so excited about Paris.

482
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:02,803
Um, I mean,
you said you were scared.

483
00:21:02,845 --> 00:21:06,557
Well, yeah, I mean, it was
good-scared, though, you know.

484
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,060
Like when
I-moved-to-New-York scared.

485
00:21:09,102 --> 00:21:12,939
Or, uh, when I-found-out-
I-was-going-to-have-Emma scared.

486
00:21:16,274 --> 00:21:18,069
But this is... fine.

487
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:20,487
This is going to be good.

488
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:28,204
You should go.

489
00:21:28,246 --> 00:21:30,248
What?

490
00:21:31,207 --> 00:21:35,461
It's what you want;
you should go.

491
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:38,131
Do you really think so?

492
00:21:38,172 --> 00:21:41,092
I really do.

493
00:21:41,134 --> 00:21:45,012
But I already told Zelner
that I would come back.

494
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,431
I'm sure he'll understand.

495
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:54,814
All right.

496
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:57,108
All right. I'm going to do it.

497
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:59,068
I'm going to go to Paris.

498
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:00,778
Yeah.

499
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,779
Yeah!

500
00:22:01,821 --> 00:22:03,823
I'm going to Paris!

501
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,908
Thank you, Ross.

502
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:07,409
Yeah, yeah.

503
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:10,246
Aw.

504
00:22:10,288 --> 00:22:12,623
Oh, I'm so happy.

505
00:22:12,665 --> 00:22:14,250
( sighs )

506
00:22:14,292 --> 00:22:15,751
Then I'm happy, too.

507
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:16,794
Aw.

508
00:22:27,096 --> 00:22:29,556
Thank you all for coming.

509
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:33,560
We're here today to pay our
respects to a wonderful agent

510
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:36,230
and a beautiful woman.

511
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:39,150
Inside.

512
00:22:39,192 --> 00:22:43,029
As Estelle's only two clients,

513
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:46,199
we would like
to say a few words.

514
00:22:48,366 --> 00:22:49,952
Dude, where's my speech?

515
00:22:49,994 --> 00:22:52,538
( gulps )

516
00:22:55,249 --> 00:22:56,458
That is entertaining.

517
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,960
Al Zeebooker, everybody!

518
00:22:58,002 --> 00:22:59,295
( scattered applause )

519
00:22:59,337 --> 00:23:02,464
Yeah.

520
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:07,053
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

